  "question": {
    "text": "Two straignt conducting plates form an angle $\\theta$ where their ends are joined. A conducting bar in contact with the plates and forming an isosceles triangle with them starts at the vertex at time $t=0$ and moves with constant velocity $\\vec{v}$ to the right as shown in figure. A magnetic field $\\vec{B}$ points out of the page. The magnitude of emf induced at $t=1$ second will be\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0000_78e6eeaf020a.png\"/><br/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Bv} \\tan \\frac{\\theta}{2}$",
